            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="LIN03" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName>Dr</roleName>
                        <forename>James</forename>
                        <surname>Lindsay</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth notBefore="1744" notAfter="1745">
                        <placeName>Scotland</placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1821-02-14"/>
                    <occupation>dissenting minister</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Dissenting minister who came from Forfarshire, Scotland. Lindsay succeeded James Fordyce (1720-1796) as preacher in Monkwell St. 
  Lindsay died delivering an animated speech at a meeting of dissenting ministers at the Dr Williams Library to discuss legislation relating to 
  English dissenters.</p>
                        <p>Lindsay is not to be confused with Lindsey which refers to <persName key="LIN03">Theophilus Lindsay</persName>, also a dissenting minister recorded in the diary.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="journalism"><title>The Times</title>, 15 February 1821 and 24 February 1821</bibl>
                    <bibl type="journalism"><title>Morning Chronicle</title>, 17 February 1821</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
